# Configuration for scripts/selfhost.sh (docs/SELF-HOSTING.md).
#
# Copy this file OUTSIDE the checkout (for example ~/ghostlink/selfhost.env),
# edit it, and pass it with --config. Format: KEY=VALUE per line; blank lines
# and lines starting with # are ignored; one pair of surrounding quotes is
# removed; a leading ~/ means your home directory. The file is read, never
# executed, so $VARIABLES are not expanded.
#
# Each service receives only the keys meant for it (by prefix, listed per
# section below) plus the values the runner derives from its state, in an
# otherwise empty environment. Keep this file private if you add the
# credential-bearing keys marked "secret" below.

# ---- Required ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Your deployment manifest (docs/DEPLOYMENTS.md). For a local validator running
# the default program build: node scripts/deployment.mjs manifest > ~/ghostlink/manifest.json
GHOSTLINK_DEPLOYMENT=~/ghostlink/manifest.json

# The RPC of the chain the manifest names. Plain HTTP only for loopback; use
# HTTPS otherwise. A provider URL with an API key in it is a secret.
RPC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8899

# Directory for all service state, keys, logs and process IDs. Must be outside
# this checkout. Created with mode 700 on the first start. Back it up (see
# docs/BACKUP-RESTORE.md) and never share it: it holds the relayer and solver
# payer keypairs and the storage encryption keys.
GHOSTLINK_STATE_DIR=~/ghostlink/state

# ---- Optional: chain and RPC ------------------------------------------------

# The chain's genesis hash. Devnet and mainnet-beta manifests already pin it.
# Unset for a localnet manifest, the first init adopts the RPC's genesis and
# records it in GHOSTLINK_STATE_DIR/genesis; later runs refuse any other chain.
# GHOSTLINK_GENESIS_HASH=

# Instead of RPC_URL: a private JSON file listing 1 to 4 endpoints with
# optional auth headers (docs/RPC-OPERATIONS.md). Secret. Required to set
# GHOSTLINK_GENESIS_HASH too when there is no RPC_URL.
# RPC_ENDPOINTS_PATH=~/ghostlink/rpc-endpoints.json

# ---- Optional: which services, ports and timing -----------------------------

# Services to run (default: all five).
# SERVICES=indexer relayer solver actions watcher

# Public HTTP ports. Each service listens on all interfaces: put a reverse
# proxy with TLS in front and firewall these ports from the internet.
# INDEXER_PORT=8787
# RELAYER_PORT=8788
# SOLVER_PORT=8789
# ACTIONS_PORT=8790
# WATCHER_PORT=8791

# Loopback-only operator ports (metrics and status); default: public port + 10000.
# RELAYER_OPERATIONS_PORT=18788
# SOLVER_OPERATIONS_PORT=18789
# ACTIONS_OPERATIONS_PORT=18790

# Seconds start waits for each service to answer /health (default 60).
# GHOSTLINK_STARTUP_SECONDS=60

# Set to 1 only when every service sits behind your own reverse proxy, so
# rate limits use X-Forwarded-For. Passed to the relayer, solver and Actions.
# TRUST_PROXY=0

# ---- Indexer (keys starting INDEXER_, plus WEBHOOK_SECRET) ------------------
# docs/INDEXER-OPERATIONS.md. The runner supplies INDEXER_GENESIS_HASH and the
# state variables.

# Milliseconds between polls, 50..30000 (default 5000).
# INDEXER_POLL_MS=5000
# Work limits per poll.
# INDEXER_PAGES_PER_TICK=4
# INDEXER_TRANSACTIONS_PER_TICK=32
# INDEXER_TICK_BUDGET_MS=10000
# INDEXER_PACE_MS=120
# Shared secret for the provider webhook that wakes the poller. Secret.
# WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ---- Relayer (keys starting RELAYER_, plus TRUST_PROXY) ---------------------
# docs/RELAYER-OPERATIONS.md. Its payer keypair is created in
# GHOSTLINK_STATE_DIR/relayer by the first init; status prints its address.
# Fund it: it pays for registrations, snapshots (network fee plus the census
# fee) and session opening, and is not ready below its reserve.

# Lamports the relayer may spend per day (default 2000000000 = 2 SOL).
# RELAYER_DAILY_BUDGET_LAMPORTS=2000000000
# Reserve below which the relayer stops taking new work (default 50000000).
# RELAYER_MIN_BALANCE_LAMPORTS=50000000
# Highest census snapshot fee it pays (default 1000000 = 0.001 SOL).
# RELAYER_MAX_SNAPSHOT_FEE_LAMPORTS=1000000
# Comma-separated origins whose pockets it opens (default: any).
# RELAYER_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://app.example.com
# Requests in flight at once (default 8).
# RELAYER_MAX_IN_FLIGHT=8

# ---- Solver (keys starting SOLVER_ or JUPITER_, plus PRICE_ACCOUNTS) --------
# docs/SOLVER-OPERATIONS.md. Its payer keypair is created in
# GHOSTLINK_STATE_DIR/solver; fund it and give it the output-token inventory
# it fills from.

# JSON map of mint -> Pyth price update account (default {}).
# PRICE_ACCOUNTS={}
# inventory (default) or the experimental jupiter-raydium-cp router.
# SOLVER_ROUTER=inventory
# SOLVER_MAX_SPREAD_BPS=100
# SOLVER_ALLOW_UNPRICED=0
# SOLVER_CREATE_POCKET_ATA=0
# SOLVER_MIN_BALANCE_LAMPORTS=5000000
# SOLVER_MAX_COMPUTE_UNITS=1400000
# SOLVER_PRIORITY_MICRO_LAMPORTS=0
# SOLVER_MAX_NETWORK_FEE_LAMPORTS=20000
# Jupiter router only: private files (secret) and the quote tolerance.
# JUPITER_API_KEY_PATH=~/ghostlink/jupiter-api-key
# JUPITER_POOLS_PATH=~/ghostlink/jupiter-pools.json
# JUPITER_SLIPPAGE_BPS=50

# ---- Actions (keys starting ACTIONS_, plus TRUST_PROXY) ---------------------
# docs/ACTIONS-OPERATIONS.md. Holds no keys and no state.

# The public origin clients reach the Actions service at (default
# http://127.0.0.1:ACTIONS_PORT). Blink links and icons point here.
# ACTIONS_BASE_URL=https://actions.example.com
# ACTIONS_MAX_IN_FLIGHT=8

# ---- Watcher (keys starting WATCHER_, plus NOTIFY_WEBHOOK, LARGE_FILL_USD_E6)
# docs/WATCHER-OPERATIONS.md. The webhook and threshold are part of the
# watcher state's scope: changing them later needs a new watcher state.

# observer (default: alerts only) or funded (also cranks timelocked changes
# with its own payer, created by init; needs WATCHER_TOTAL_BUDGET_LAMPORTS).
# WATCHER_MODE=observer
# WATCHER_TOTAL_BUDGET_LAMPORTS=100000000
# WATCHER_MAX_FEE_LAMPORTS=20000
# HTTPS (or loopback HTTP) endpoint that receives alerts; unset prints them
# to the watcher log. Secret if it carries a token.
# NOTIFY_WEBHOOK=https://alerts.example.com/ghostlink
# Large-fill alert threshold in micro-dollars (default 100000000 = $100).
# LARGE_FILL_USD_E6=100000000
# WATCHER_POLL_MS=5000
# WATCHER_PAGES_PER_TICK=4
# WATCHER_TRANSACTIONS_PER_TICK=32
# WATCHER_DELIVERIES_PER_TICK=32
# WATCHER_TICK_BUDGET_MS=10000
